  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Still we rise: equal power, lasting peace</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The overall objective of the project is to reinforce the centrality of the Women Peace and Security (WPS) agenda in national and international peace and security processes. More specifically, the project aims to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;strengthen the agency and resilience of women and their organisations in peace processes and/or conflict prevention and resolution strategies (outcome 1); and&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;enhance the recognition and influence of women peacebuilders in formal and informal peace and security processes (outcome 2).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The programme will be implemented in four geographic contexts: the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), Sudan, Palestine and Syria. These have been selected to represent a diverse geographic focus based on strategic priorities for the EU and on the consortium&#xbf;s existing networks. Most importantly, all four contexts are facing decisive moments when it comes to peace and security processes, with time-sensitive opportunities to ensure that women peacebuilders play a formative role in these.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
